::U2P01::Which is a health-related fitness component? {=Muscular endurance ~Agility ~Reaction time ~Speed}

::U2P02::Which activity is primarily aerobic? {=A sustained brisk walk ~A 10-second sprint ~One explosive jump ~A brief maximal effort}

::U2P03::Which term describes how hard the body works? {=Intensity ~Duration ~Frequency ~Recovery}

::U2P04::Repeated low-resistance contractions primarily emphasize what? {=Muscular endurance ~Muscular strength only ~Reaction time ~Agility}

::U2P05::Which activity best supports flexibility? {=A controlled joint-range routine ~A sprint ~A response drill ~A power jump}

::U2P06::In FITT, increasing a session from 15 to 20 minutes changes what? {=Time ~Type ~Frequency ~Intensity}

::U2P07::Which monitoring combination provides stronger intensity evidence? {=Heart rate, talk test, RPE, and observations ~Sweating alone ~A device alone ~Duration alone}

::U2P08::Which is safest when movement quality declines? {=Reduce resistance or modify the movement ~Continue to failure ~Increase speed ~Ignore form}

::U2P09::One difficult session is best interpreted as what? {=A single data point requiring more evidence ~A complete trend ~Proof of failure ~A reason for maximal progression}

::U2P10::Which plan is strongest? {=Goal-matched FITT, gradual progression, recovery, monitoring, and modification ~Maximum effort daily ~No recovery ~Unrelated monitoring}

